  "worked_solution": "Since the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=-3$ underestimates the values of the function, we have\n\n$$\nL(x)<f(x),\n$$\n\nthat is, the line $L(x)$ must be below the graph of $f(x)$ near the point  $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the function must be concave up in the neighborhood of $x=-3.$",
